ion.   e.g. premp-v2   Note that we should explictly assign which version of key do we use.  Because we fetch the EC firmware and touchpad firmware from the same version and pack to a single tarball, we might face the situation that only touchpad firmware is upgraded. Therefore we cannot use EC firmware version as the tarball file name. Now the file naming is:   &lt;Base name&gt;_&lt;version&gt;_&lt;signed_key&gt;.tbz2 For example:   hammer_9959.0.0_premp-v2.tbz2  BUG=b:65230801 TEST=Run `./pack_firmware.sh -b poppy -v 9959.0.0 -s premp-v2`      and check the tarball is generated  Change-Id: I52bbf47d4b7230e0bf6fdf8742e12ba878d6c690 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/674514 Commit-Ready: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="674514" owner_email="akahuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/14/674514/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia74bc69e1ae42f877b72945eba8e2fc701e4c2d1" commit="12d26af3ce92bfc4c178abe1349542354921cb9a" commit_message="autotest: add cr50_stress_flaky  There are some issues with cr50 tests that require an update/rollback. We need to workout these issues before we can add the tests to the main suite. If a test is in the main suite and leaves cr50 running the wrong version then all following tests in the suite will be invalid.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: Ia74bc69e1ae42f877b72945eba8e2fc701e4c2d1 Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/685357 Reviewed-by: Kevin Shelton &lt;kmshelton@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="685357" owner_email="mruthven@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="c